## Summary

I implemented customer-code de-duplication in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode`.

The existing code built the customer code as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. I split that into a base value and added a `deduplicateCustomerCode` step:

```java
private String generateCustomerCode(Owner owner) {
    String base = regionFor(owner) + "-" + hash8(owner);
    return deduplicateCustomerCode(base);
}

private String deduplicateCustomerCode(String base) {
    Set<String> existing = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .map(Owner::getCustomerCode)
        .filter(code -> code != null)
        .collect(java.util.stream.Collectors.toSet());
    if (!existing.contains(base)) {
        return base;
    }
    int n = 2;
    while (existing.contains(base + "-" + n)) {
        n++;
    }
    return base + "-" + n;
}
```

When the computed code collides with an existing owner's `customerCode`, it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n ≥ 2` that yields a code not already in use, and returns that de-duplicated code. When there's no collision, the base code is returned unchanged. This runs before the owner is persisted (in `saveOwner`), consistent with the other pre-persist derivations.

